<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT MUST SIT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <QuickAction>
        breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading error "unable to find
        matching parent xml file". Precedent: Broker_Protection_Access.permissionset-meta.xml.

        DISPOSITION LOI ONLY. One half of the sell-side negotiation LOOP.

        WHY A LOOP NEEDS EXPLICIT BUTTONS AT ALL. The sell-side path is
        Received -> Under Review -> Countered by DPEG -> Counter Received from Buyer ->
        Executed, and the document says the negotiation "goes round until both sides are
        agreed". Countered by DPEG <-> Counter Received from Buyer is therefore a CYCLE, and
        RecordStageAdvanceService holds a LINEAR Map<String,String> NEXT_STAGE per object -
        one key, one value - which cannot express a back-edge. Advance Stage walks the line;
        these two actions drive the loop. This action supplies the BACK-EDGE (the one edge a
        linear map provably cannot reach): Counter Received from Buyer -> Countered by DPEG.

        PATTERN: headless quick action backed by an LWC, mirroring NDA__c.Mark_Declined from
        Tranche 3A. actionSubtype Action + type LightningWebComponent + an empty template is
        what makes it headless; the LWC is invoked on click, owns its own confirm and toasts,
        and must call getRecordNotifyChange on success because the write is imperative Apex
        and happens behind LDS's back (ARCHITECTURE.md §5, the middle column of the
        three-guard table).

        🔴 THE LWC BUNDLE IS NOT IN THIS TRANCHE'S DECLARATIVE SCOPE. The expected name is
        lwc/loiMarkCounteredByDpeg. It is the developer's file. This quick action WILL FAIL
        DEPLOY until that bundle exists - deploy them together, not in either order alone.

        🔴 IT ALSO NEEDS AN APEX ALLOW-LIST ENTRY. RecordStageAdvanceService exposes advance()
        only; an explicit target must be added to the LOI DISPOSITION explicit-target set
        ('Countered by DPEG'), record-type-scoped. Record-type picklist restriction is UI-ONLY
        and is NOT enforced by Apex DML, so an object-level allow-list would let this value be
        written onto an ACQUISITION LOI, whose Stage__c does not carry it. The allow-list is
        the only thing that actually refuses that.

        LABEL WORDING IS THE TARGET STAGE, DELIBERATELY. Unlike LOI__c.Advance_Stage - which
        backs a derived hop and must stay generic - this action has exactly ONE target, so the
        label can name it and the confirm prompt can too.
    -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Countered by DPEG</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>loiMarkCounteredByDpeg</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
